# A policy that does nothing at all.
#
# It compiles, Vault stores it, and it shows up in the policy list looking like
# a control -- but the rule is the literal `true`, so every request passes. That
# is what the audit report's "always evaluates to true" finding exists to catch,
# so do not add a real condition here.
//
// Both comment syntaxes appear on purpose: the check strips "#" and "//" before
// looking at the rule, and a comment above it must not hide it.

main = rule { true }
